# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Both point at the NestJS API (port 3000).

# Used by Server Components (`lib/api.ts`). Server-side only.
API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Used by the navbar search typeahead, which fetches from the BROWSER — a
# server-only var is `undefined` there, so this one is required.
#
# Next inlines `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` at build time: change it and restart the dev
# server, or the old value stays compiled into the client bundle.
#
# Testing from a phone on the LAN? This must be the dev machine's LAN IP, not
# `localhost` — the phone cannot resolve `localhost` to your machine. Point it
# at the API's port (3000), e.g. http://192.168.1.10:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.31.53:3001

